    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3946" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλείπ-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anointer</i>: hence (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλείφω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			) <i>trainer</i> in gymnasia, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1106b1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				27.7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4224.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.133b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀθληταὶ τῆς ἀρετῆς μὴ ψεύσαντες
					τοὺς ἀλείπτας νόμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.409
				</span></i>
			; <i>teacher</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πολιτικῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς κακίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					1.298
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Lat.
				<i>aliptes, bath-attendant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Juv.
				6.422
			</span></i>.</div>
